# Wave W17-Q (Route 123): berry row marker — a berry-row end marker at the fields’ edge: a short post carrying a cluster of ripe berries at its head, marking where one tended row ends and the road’s jurisdiction begins (design: the Berry Master’s fields perfume the whole south bend; the rows are ended with markers, not fences). On master turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Yamato’s berrytree/berrycrate by register: a tended field’s row-end post, not a wild climb’s tree or a picker’s crate.
